Subject: [PATCH] fix(gates): address CodeRabbit review on B2 (fail-closed
 hardening)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four review threads on PR #381:

1. runner.js — live per-gate log printed "PASS" for a SKIPPED gate
   (same false-green class B2 fixes, one layer earlier). New gateLogMark
   labels skipped gates SKIP in the live log, not just the summary.
2. preflight.js — fail-OPEN risk: `changeSet.resolved === false` only
   caught an explicit false; an override omitting `resolved` passed
   through vacuously. Now `!changeSet.resolved` — anything not explicitly
   resolved fails CLOSED.
3. preflight.js — the file list re-resolved its own diff base via
   getChangedFiles (could pick a different branch). Now diffs against the
   SAME resolved baseRef (merge-base ... HEAD), keeping the blast radius
   consistent with the resolved base. Drops the now-unused import.
4. preflight.js — extracted the nested template literal (SonarCloud).

Tests added: skipped-gate live log = SKIP; fail-closed when `resolved`
omitted; diff uses the resolved base.

Kernel: 12b00157-07a2-4431-99c2-14dd640eb225

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
